<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Egor Dëmin on a Rookie Contract?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Dëmin is paid <strong>$7.23m</strong> because he was the eighth pick in 2025, and nothing he does for four years will change it.</p>
<ul>
<li>Draft slot fixes first-round salaries, so his figure was settled the moment his name was called.</li>
<li>He’s a 6’8″ guard who runs an offense from that height, which is the rarest thing about him and the reason he went in the lottery.</li>
<li>His outside shooting was the question at college and remains the thing clubs are waiting on.</li>
<li>He arrived at 19 from Russia by way of Spain and one American college season, so his development has happened across three basketball cultures.</li>
<li>Both remaining seasons are club options, so Brooklyn keeps a decision point every October.</li>
</ul>
<p>He’ll be 22 if the contract runs its full length, which is young for a player entering restricted free agency.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
